  "DeepSWE v1.1": "GPT-6.1 Sol per level from OpenAI's launch-page chart; its GPT-6 Astra and GPT-6 Sol points equal charts.py exactly. Sonnet 5.5 has no per-level DeepSWE anywhere: only 71.0% (5-trial avg, default config = max effort) in its system card §8.3. The DeepSWE leaderboard (deepswe.datacurve.ai) lists none of GPT-6.1 Sol, Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1.",
  "FrontierCode 1.1 Main": "All 7 models from Cognition's leaderboard data file (field new_score, Main set). Matches charts.py for every existing point except Fable 5.1 low: Cognition 49.8 vs charts.py 52.8 (52.8 came from Anthropic's Opus 5.5 page). Sonnet 5.5 peaks at xhigh 52.1 and drops to 46.2 at max.",
  "AA Coding Agent Index": "No v1.4 per-level numbers for GPT-6.1 Sol or Sonnet 5.5: OpenAI's 6.1 Sol page does not chart it, and AA's coding-agents page shows only the live index per agent/harness, not v1.4 per effort level.",
  "SWE-Bench Pro": "Sonnet 5.5 81.3% at max (system card Table 8.1.A). OpenAI published no SWE-Bench Pro for GPT-6.1 Sol (launch page and system-card addendum checked).",
  "LiveCodeBench": "Vals AI's LiveCodeBench page was last updated 2026-09-01; neither GPT-6.1 Sol nor Sonnet 5.5 is on it. AA records carry no livecodebench value for either.",
  "AA-Briefcase": "Long-horizon knowledge-work Elo from AA (briefcaseBreakdown.overall.elo). Full coverage: all 7 models at every level they run. Anthropic's Sonnet 5.5 page charts the same benchmark (Sonnet 5.5 low..max 1264, 1461, 1634, 1746, 1811), close to AA's live values.",
  "CursorBench 4.0": "Cursor's own leaderboard, run in Cursor's production harness, 5 effort levels per model. Covers GPT-5.6 Sol, Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5. No GPT-6 family model is listed.",
  "GDP.pdf": "AA's GDP.pdf (gdpPdfAllPass): professional Q&A over complex PDFs. Full 7-model coverage. OpenAI's 6.1 Sol launch page charts the same values for GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Astra and GPT-6 Sol. Scores are flat across effort levels (~25-32%), so the chart will show little effort dependence.",
  "aa_existing_metrics": "AA live values for every existing AA metric, all 7 models, for cross-checking charts.py and filling GPT-6.1 Sol and Sonnet 5.5. ARC-AGI-2: GPT-6 Sol is now on the ARC Prize leaderboard (was absent at the last fetch); Sonnet 5.5 is not yet.",
  "skipped": "OSWorld: OpenAI reports OSWorld 2.0 offline (GPT models only), Anthropic reports OSWorld 2.1 partial (Claude only, max) - not comparable. Terminal-Bench Science 0.1: AA has max-only for most models; OpenAI and Anthropic launch pages disagree on the same points (e.g. Astra max 68.1 vs 64.6)."
